From 48fa7fbc4e55598d7dd4bd2c4e4d08eaa1ab269d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: verkur46 <mohamadrezasahami1999@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 00:10:15 +0330
Subject: [PATCH 178/230] fix(timeline): 10 visual polish fixes on the event
 timeline
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Rewrites the TimelineList render so the timeline reads as a coloured,
scorable match story rather than a monochrome list. All changes are
visual — no data flow, no API contract, no i18n keys changed.

- FIX 1: marker dots are h-8 filled circles with a 2px border in the event
  tone (volt for goal, gold for card, line for sub/var, muted for kickoff/
  halftime/fulltime/other), drawn from SVG icons / unicode glyphs, never
  emoji.
- FIX 2: continuous vertical rail with a 2px gradient that fades at both
  ends (transparent → border-subtle → transparent) so the line reads as a
  timeline spine, not a hard stick.
- FIX 3: chip tone is a ChipTone-union map (volt/gold/live/danger/muted) so
  goal→volt, yellow card→gold, red card→live, sub/var/kickoff/halftime/
  fulltime→muted — one source of truth, passed straight to Chip.
- FIX 4: goal cards get a 3px volt start edge (border-s-[3px] border-s-volt)
  so the scorer's side is visible at a glance.
- FIX 5: card and substitution cards get a 3px edge in their tone (gold for
  yellow, live for red, line for sub), and the card body gets a matching
  wash tint (volt/gold/live at 8%) so each moment reads as a coloured band.
- FIX 6: structural markers (kickoff/halftime/fulltime) render as dashed,
  borderless, transparent cards; halftime renders as a centred divider with
  a rounded-full pill carrying "Half time · N–N" and a dashed horizontal
  rule beneath it.
- FIX 7: every goal carries a scoreline badge (ms-auto, volt-tinted, font-bold)
  showing the score that goal produced (prefix count of timeline goals), so a
  goal reads "Goal — Cole Palmer · 1–0" rather than just "Goal — Cole Palmer".
- FIX 8: the newest live event's marker gets the timeline-live-pulse class
  (1.6s coral ring pulse) — only applied when liveMinute is passed, so
  finished matches stay quiet.
- FIX 9: clustered band — two+ events sharing the same minute display get a
  rounded-e-card band with a 50%-surface tint and -me-2/ps-2 bleed so they
  read as "this minute was busy" instead of isolated rows.
- FIX 10: participant row uses dot separators (h-1 w-1 rounded-full dots)
  between names so it reads cleanly in RTL.

DOM-verified at 390x720 on match 401882839: 21 timeline rows, 20 markers
with 2px borders, 5 goal cards with volt edges + 5 scoreline badges (1–0,
2–0, 3–0, 3–1, 4–1), 4 cards with gold edges, 1 halftime divider with pill
"Half time · 2–0" + dashed rule, 10 clustered-band rows, 14 participant
dots, chip labels [Kickoff, Card, Card, Goal, Goal, Substitution, …], and
the timeline-live-pulse keyframe confirmed working via injected test element.

Co-Authored-By: Codebuff <noreply@codebuff.com>
